WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.642 --> 00:00:06.278
Walmart noticed something strange.

2
00:00:06.470 --> 00:00:08.509
People weren't just buying its rotisserie chicken.

3
00:00:08.710 --> 00:00:11.815
They were joking about carrying the bag like a fashion accessory.

4
00:00:14.475 --> 00:00:16.495
Fifteen thousand social mentions later,

5
00:00:16.750 --> 00:00:18.472
the deli bag had a fan base.

6
00:00:20.030 --> 00:00:21.449
Instead of ignoring the joke,

7
00:00:21.567 --> 00:00:22.688
the brand made it real.

8
00:00:22.850 --> 00:00:26.510
A chicken-shaped purse. Complete with the packaging-inspired design.

9
00:00:27.641 --> 00:00:30.151
Same type. Same colors. Same chicken.

10
00:00:30.370 --> 00:00:31.344
Then they added a strap.

11
00:00:33.442 --> 00:00:36.134
Two flavors: Traditional, with purple trim.

12
00:00:36.350 --> 00:00:38.155
And Lemon Pepper, in orange.

13
00:00:40.043 --> 00:00:42.352
And the price? Just five ninety-seven.

14
00:00:42.550 --> 00:00:45.362
The same price as the rotisserie chicken that inspired

15
00:00:45.442 --> 00:00:50.494
it. Five thousand purses. One drop. September first.

16
00:00:51.242 --> 00:00:53.727
Plus matching bag charms, because of course.

17
00:00:55.192 --> 00:00:58.652
When it launched online, the purse sold out in just ninety minutes.

18
00:01:01.442 --> 00:01:02.677
A second drop followed.

19
00:01:02.890 --> 00:01:06.361
Resale listings climbed to several times the original price.

20
00:01:06.766 --> 00:01:07.954
The joke had become merch.

21
00:01:08.162 --> 00:01:09.304
The merch had become a moment.

22
00:01:10.456 --> 00:01:13.752
Sometimes, your next big product isn't hiding in a boardroom.

23
00:01:13.950 --> 00:01:15.861
It's hiding inside a customer joke.
